\n52\t    \"postcss\": \"^8.4.49\",\n53\t    \"size-limit\": \"^12.0.1\",\n54\t    \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.2.1\",\n55\t    \"typescript\": \"^5.7.0\",\n56\t    \"vitest\": \"^4.1.0\"\n57\t  }\n58\t}\n59\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e214bee3-232f-4b1b-8118-dc441d3da087","uuid":"c298c2b1-4461-4b12-a9cf-f1fccba481c4","timestamp":"2026-04-14T05:44:04.629Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\package.json","content":"{\n  \"name\": \"pelangi-website\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"next dev --turbo\",\n    \"build\": \"next build\",\n    \"start\": \"next start\",\n    \"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n    \"analyze\": \"ANALYZE=true npm run build\",\n    \"size\": \"size-limit\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@marsidev/react-turnstile\": \"^1.5.0\",\n    \"@next/third-parties\": \"^16.1.6\",\n    \"@sentry/nextjs\": \"^10.43.0\",\n    \"@serwist/next\": \"^9.5.6\",\n    \"@stripe/react-stripe-js\": \"^5.6.1\",\n    \"@stripe/stripe-js\": \"^8.9.0\",\n    \"@tailwindcss/typography\": \"^0.5.19\",\n    \"@vercel/speed-insights\": \"^2.0.0\",\n    \"babel-plugin-react-compiler\": \"^19.0.0-beta-af1b7da-20250417\",\n    \"fuse.js\": \"^7.1.0\",\n    \"next\": \"^16.1.6\",\n    \"react\": \"^19.2.0\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^19.2.0\",\n    \"resend\": \"^6.9.3\",\n    \"serwist\": \"^9.5.6\",\n    \"stripe\": \"^20.4.1\",\n    \"web-vitals\": \"^4.2.4\",\n    \"yet-another-react-lightbox\": \"^3.29.1\"\n  },\n  \"size-limit\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Homepage initial JS (gzip)\",\n      \"path\": \".next/static/chunks/*.js\",\n      \"limit\": \"250 kB\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@axe-core/playwright\": \"^4.11.1\",\n    \"@lhci/cli\": \"^0.15.1\",\n    \"@next/bundle-analyzer\": \"^16.1.6\",\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.58.2\",\n    \"@size-limit/file\": \"^12.0.1\",\n    \"@tailwindcss/postcss\": \"^4.2.1\",\n    \"@types/node\": \"^22.0.0\",\n    \"@types/react\": \"^19.0.0\",\n    \"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.0.0\",\n    \"eslint\": \"^9.39.4\",\n    \"eslint-config-next\": \"^16.1.6\",\n    \"postcss\": \"^8.4.49\",\n    \"size-limit\": \"^12.0.1\",\n    \"tailwindcss\": \"^4.2.1\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.7.0\",\n    \"vitest\": \"^4.1.0\"\n  }\n}\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WQzKEs1bh5Xs7vJ4K6RFp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, there's no Radix UI Select installed. So the project is using a native `<select>` element in BookingForm.tsx.\n\nNow let me understand what the story is asking for:\n1. \"Language switcher and any filter dropdowns use <select> with appearance: base-select where custom Select was used\"\n2. The story mentions converting from custom Radix UI Select components to native select\n3. Need to style with appearance: base-select CSS for Chrome 130+\n4. Need @supports guard for progressive enhancement\n5. Ensure WCAG 4.1.2 compliance (keyboard and screen reader support)\n\nLooking at the code:\n- LanguageSwitcher is using buttons (not a select)\n- BlogFilter is using buttons (not a select)\n- BookingForm has a native select element for room type\n\nThe note says this was \"skipped\" because \"CSS appearance: base-select is experimental and not in stable Chrome/Firefox\". However, the assignment still says to implement it.\n\nThe story seems to be asking us to create styled native select elements. Let me think about the implementation:\n\n1. The BookingForm select needs to be enhanced with the `appearance: base-select` CSS styling\n2. We could convert the LanguageSwitcher from buttons to a native select if desired (though the story doesn't explicitly require this)\n3. BlogFilter filtering could use a select instead of buttons (though the story doesn't explicitly require this either)\n\nLooking at the acceptance criteria more carefully:\n- \"Language switcher and any filter dropdowns use <select>\" - this suggests we should at least look at these\n- \"where custom Select was used\" - but there is no custom Select used in the codebase\n\nThe key acceptance criterion is: \"Styled select matches brand design system (border-radius, colours, font)\" with a \"@supports (appearance: base-select) guard\"\n\nSo the implementation should:\n1. Create CSS for styling native select elements using `appearance: base-select`\n\n\n2. Add this CSS to globals.css with @supports guard\n3. Apply this to the existing select in BookingForm and any other selects\n\nI need to modify globals.css to add the select styling with progressive enhancement, then apply the class to BookingForm's select element. The CSS should match the brand design system with proper dark mode and forced colors support.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":85315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e214bee3-232f-4b1b-8118-dc441d3da087","uuid":"74b2c5c7-744e-4c52-aea5-0dde079a24c9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WQzKEs1bh5Xs7vJ4K6RFp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough context. Let me create the implementation plan.\n\n## Current State\n- Project is a Next.js/React website with native `<select>` elements (e.g., BookingForm.tsx)\n- No Radix UI Select is currently installed or used\n- Current select styling uses Tailwind classes (border-stone-500, bg-stone-50, etc.)\n- globals.css has existing styled form elements with forced-colors and prefers-contrast support\n\n## Problem Identified\nThe story asks to adopt the new CSS `appearance: base-select` property for styled native `<select>` elements with proper progressive enhancement. This requires:\n1. Creating CSS for appearance: base-select styling\n2. Adding @supports guard for browsers that don't support it\n3. Applying it to existing select elements\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\n    \"site/src/app/globals.css\",\n    \"site/src/components/BookingForm.tsx\"\n  ],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 45\n}\n</plan>\n\nLet me execute the plan by first adding the CSS styling in globals.css:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":85315,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1078},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e214bee3-232f-4b1b-8118-dc441d3da087","uuid":"c90430a6-d4bd-422e-b03d-2d304fcedcaa"}
